ngs to a group of more  than 1200 priests nuns and missionaries  who have abandoned neutrality in this  race to support robredo  during a recent sunday mass in his  church balthazar referred to an  aggressive social media campaign by  supporters of marcos jr he accuses them  of trying to rewrite history  it was said that the martial law years  was the golden age balthazar says adding  maybe only for the cronies maybe only  for the marcos family  but in a country which is 80 catholic  there's controversy over where priests  should draw the line an official in the  catholic bishops conference told dw  priests must speak the truth about human  rights violations that happened during  martial law but they should not be  campaigning for any particular candidate  this parishioner in baltizard's church  was critical of him publicly taking  sides i agree that the priests shouldn't  be campaigning or shouldn't be biased to  any candidates father balthazar plays  down those concerns the role of the  catholic church  we have to be the promoters of good news  the gospel  that's why we have to promote the good  candidates and not the bad one  balthazar has even outfitted a van for  his campaigning he drives around his  province showing solidarity with the  robredo faithful and trying to convert  supporters of ferdinand marcos jr  he says to this man i'm here trying to  explain to you if you could reconsider  your choice  the response  i'm sorry my decision is final i am for  marcos sad to say uh they are easily  swayed with the tick tocks with the  youtube with the social media they are  watching  and so he keeps on campaigning  as the clock ticks down to election day  hoping that enough votes go his  candidate's way  and joining me now for more from manila  is journalist jc gottinger jc fernand  marcos jr is currently leading in  opinion polls despite his family's  legacy and a conviction for income tax  evasion uh  how and what is his offer to filipinos  well ferdinand marcos jr we call him  bong bong first up he's teamed up with  the daughter of the current president  rodrigo duterte her name is sarah  duterte and they are running in tandem  so the voter base of duterte's and of  the marcoses have kind of joined  together and that is the premise of  their pitch to the country to voters  which is unity they call themselves the  unit team and in their sorties and all  of their campaign materials they have  been just promoting this idea of unity  unity about what and unity of whom they  don't exactly explain  but they're drawing from this vague idea  of the  country's politics being so fraught with  conflict and opposing views um the  atmosphere being so toxic so enough  marcos is promising we're gonna get rid  of all that we are going to to uh  establish unity in the country and with  unity we are going to rise up again so  he gives these vague promises of rising  back from whatever crisis the  philippines is in  um without saying it he is hearkening  back to  uh nostalgia for the so-called good old  days of his father's regime of course  you know  nostalgia makes things look rosy and  there is this machinery there is this  campaign of this information that have  basically whitewashed the marcos  family's history and have highlighted  you know the fact that they live like  royalty they have come to be associated  with opulence and big ticket projects  and flashy  uh infrastructure development during  uh the time of demarcus of course  without mentioning the fact that the  country went into bad debt during those  times and all of those things the  country plunging into poverty all of  these  are hidden behind the screen this battle  cry of unity and the promise of going  back to the good old days more  prosperous days yes  jesse i do want to talk to you about  that particularly about this veneer that  is being propagated uh on social media  but before that i'd just like to talk  about his challenger who is currently  running second in the race in the  opinion polls vice president current  vice president leni robredo what is her  pitch to voters  well her promise is the exact opposite  of what marco says what  marcos jr is promising and that is a  a government free of corruption a  government that works properly in  service of the country so her tagline  her pitch to the country is uh it's  called  which basically translates to with a  government that's honest everyone's  lives uh is going to improve so for her  uh her basic her although she does have  many programs that she wants to put  forward uh her main pitch is that we're  going to fix this government we're going  to weed out corruption and if we do that  if we only just make things make the  bureaucracy work properly then you will  see that everyone's lives is going to  improve  uh i'd like to go back to the point  about misinformation that you were  making earlier that also the report that  we've played  for our viewers is also making about  social media misinformation during this  election uh in fact late last year i had  spoken to nobel prize winning journalist  and rappler ceo maria rasa about this  and i'd just like to play for our  viewers what she said to us then  35 years after the marcos family was was  tossed out of the philippines by a  people power revolt  ferdinand marcos jr bongbong  is running for president so you know in  2019 rappler actually exposed the  networks of disinformation that had been  created to chip away at history to  reorient history and i can share that i  can share the links with you but you  know this is going to be a battle for  facts and we're going to have to make  sure that facts win and in order to do  that these american social media  platforms are going to have to put guard  rails and prioritize facts  jesse of course maria was referring to  facebook particularly which is so  popular in the philippines but the  question remains have guardrails  been put up across social media so facts  can be shared and 